From 1a325e5009785ddcafbc67db33763e27b044f83e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dev <dev@example.local>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 22:20:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] feat: Search canned responses by short code and content
 in the reply box

Typing "/" in the reply box now opens a searchable canned response
dropdown:

- The full list is fetched once when the dropdown opens and filtered on
  the client, so the content can be searched as well as the short code
  and typing no longer fires an API request per keystroke.
- Filtering is case-insensitive and debounced (150ms). Short code
  matches are listed before content matches.
- The matching text is highlighted in both the short code and the
  content, rendered as text nodes instead of v-html.
- Up/Down (and Ctrl-P/Ctrl-N) move the selection with wrap-around and
  keep the selected item scrolled into view, Enter inserts it, Escape
  closes the dropdown.
- An empty state is shown while loading, when nothing matches the
  search, and when the account has no canned responses yet.

The dropdown is now anchored to the top of the reply box with CSS
instead of an offset computed from the number of results, and talks to
the reply box through select/close events.
